I have updated `.github/mcp-config.json` to include the GitHub Copilot MCP server configuration with the required authentication mapping. 

The configuration now explicitly includes the `env` block that forwards the `$GITHUB_TOKEN` from the environment to the MCP server:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/",
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_TOKEN": "$GITHUB_TOKEN"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This aligns with the `anthropics/claude-code-action` requirements, ensuring that the token is securely passed to the MCP process at runtime to successfully authenticate with the `api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/` endpoint.

