`cross_fill` would hang indefinitely when the 8-neighbor trace produced more than 255 boundary points. The loop variable `i` was `uint8`, so it wrapped to 0 after 255 and the condition `i < total_num` (a `uint16` that can reach 360) was always true — infinite loop. A secondary bug: accessing `dir[i+7]` without bounding the loop allowed out-of-bounds reads near the end of the array.

## Changes

- **`uint8 i` → `uint16 i`** in both `for` loops inside `cross_fill` — eliminates the overflow wraparound
- **Loop condition `i < total_num` → `i + 7 < total_num`** — prevents `dir[i+3]`, `dir[i+5]`, `dir[i+7]` from reading past the end of the array

```cpp
// Before
uint8 i;
for (i = 1; i < total_num_l; i++)          // wraps at 255 → infinite loop
    if (... && dir_l[i + 7] == 6)          // OOB when i near total_num_l

// After
uint16 i;
for (i = 1; i + 7 < total_num_l; i++)      // safe upper bound
    if (... && dir_l[i + 7] == 6)
```

PvP mode had a hardcoded 3-bot spawn and rendered a progress bar for every bot, making the HUD unbounded as enemy count grows.

## Changes

- **Enemy count slider** (`index.html` + `game.js`): New `👾 Enemies` slider (1–10, default 3) in the start menu below the Race Distance slider. Wired via `_initPvpEnemySlider()` using the same pattern as the goal-distance slider; persists as `_pvpEnemyCount`.
- **Dynamic bot spawning** (`startPvpRun`): Replaced hardcoded `offsets = [-28, 0, 28]` with computed even spacing across `_pvpEnemyCount` bots.
- **Expanded bot pool**: `BOT_NAMES` and `BOT_COLORS` extended from 3 to 10 entries to cover the full slider range.
- **HUD capped at 4 bars** (`_renderPvpOverlay`): Now shows the player + the 3 highest-distance bots at any given moment, regardless of total enemy count.

```js
// Before – all bots rendered
const racers = [
  { name: 'YOU', dist: this.distance, ... },
  ...this.pvpBots.map(b => ({ ... })),
];

// After – player + top 3 by distance
const topBots = this.pvpBots.slice().sort((a, b) => b.distance - a.distance).slice(0, 3);
const racers  = [
  { name: 'YOU', dist: this.distance, ... },
  ...topBots.map(b => ({ ... })),
];
```

